{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>While YHWH had compassion on him.</b> Even though he escaped on the merit of Abraham, as it says: <b>וַיִּזְכֹּר אֱלֹהִים אֶת אַבְרָהָם וַיִּשְׁלַח אֶת לוֹט מִתּוֹךְ הַהֲפֵכָה</b> (Genesis 19:29), yet since he lingered and delayed after the angels' warning, he deserved to perish — but compassion was upon him, for his delay was not in rebellion or treachery, but from indolence and a bewildered soul."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:48.589030422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}